{
  "0": "Interest aggregation: replace the current readout with the padding-masked mean of the final three valid GRU states, using all valid states when fewer than three exist. This may retain immediate intent while reducing sensitivity to a noisy final interaction. Preserve history selection, embeddings, GRU topology, scoring, loss and optimizer. Apply across all four categories and mirror the readout in the predictor writer.",
  "1": "Sequence modeling: use only the latest 30 causal interactions per prediction prefix, preserving chronological order and retaining shorter histories intact. A bounded recent context may reduce stale-interest interference, particularly in Electronics, while limiting recurrent computation. Preserve embeddings, GRU topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Apply identical truncation during training and generated prediction across all four categories.",
  "2": "Network architecture: apply layer normalization to each GRU gate's combined preactivation before its sigmoid or tanh, retaining the existing hidden width and recurrent depth. Stabilizing gate activation scales may improve learning on sparse histories without increasing sequence length. Preserve features, embeddings, history selection, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Train one model per category and reproduce the modified GRU in the predictor writer.",
  "3": "Feature construction: multiply each existing input item embedding by 1 + 0.1*log(1 + min(c, 9)), where c counts that item's earlier occurrences in the available causal prefix. This fixed repeat-frequency feature may distinguish persistent preferences from isolated interactions without adding embedding tables or a separate scorer. Preserve history selection, GRU topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer; compute the same feature in generated prediction for all four categories."
}
